## API Quick Reference

| Endpoint | Method | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `/api/etl-trigger/discover?identifier=CEBU-CP-DEFAULT` | `GET` | Inspect remote crontab on ETL server without executing |
| `/api/etl-trigger/pipelines` | `GET` | List all configured pipelines from `etljobs.yml` |
| `/api/etl-trigger/queue-status?identifier=CEBU-CP-DEFAULT` | `GET` | Check sender queue table depth for pipeline/site |
| `/api/etl-trigger/trigger-if-queued?identifier=CEBU-CP-DEFAULT` | `POST` | Queue-aware trigger: only runs cron if queue has items |
| `/api/etl-trigger/trigger-pipeline?pipelineKey=CEBU-CP-DEFAULT&rerunPeriodMinutes=5` | `POST` | Trigger pipeline execution via SSH with queue-aware rerun |
| `/api/etl-trigger/status` | `GET` | Health, dryRun status, server count, and pipeline count |
| `/api/dashboard/pipelines` | `GET` | Dashboard pipeline configuration snapshot |
| `/api/senders/info?senderId=...` | `GET` | Fetch sender name, port, and source from `dtp_sender` with YAML fallback |
| `/api/etl-trigger/discover-by-port?port=...` | `GET` | Discover remote crontab setup matching ONLY the unique port |
| `/api/etl-trigger/trigger-by-port?port=...` | `POST` | Execute crontab setup matching ONLY the unique port via SSH |

