### 3. Automated Post-Queue Trigger Flow

When a batch of files is staged and dispatched:
1. `SenderDispatchService.pushGroup(...)` executes:
   ```sql
   INSERT INTO DTP_SENDER_QUEUE_ITEM (id, id_metadata, id_data, id_sender, record_created) VALUES (...)
   ```
2. Immediately upon successful insertion (`!success.isEmpty()`), `triggerEtlAfterQueueInsert(...)` runs.
3. It resolves the sender port (from `DTP_SENDER`), locates the configured pipeline (e.g. `CZ4-CZ2-KLARF-DEFECT-Si`), and launches the Command Processor via SSH:
   ```bash
   /apps/fecim/cz4/command-processor/bin/single_launcher.sh /apps/fecim/cz4/command-processor/xml/64566_CZ2_Defect_Klarf18_Si_Sender.xml
   ```
4. CP immediately consumes the newly inserted items from `DTP_SENDER_QUEUE_ITEM` without waiting for the next cron cycle!

