## Part 4: Stepper Step 1 Pre-Flight Exensio Check Alignment with Exensio Monitoring

### 1. Requirements & Problem Statement
- **Prior Pre-Check Issue**:
  - Stepper Step 1 lot verification was trying Oracle **raw-SQL** (`POST /v1/key/raw-sql`) by default, querying tables (`op_log`, `df_export`, `wf_log`, etc.) with complex joins, which frequently failed with 500 / 403 / syntax errors or 30-60 second timeouts.
  - If raw-SQL timed out or failed, it fell back to Snowflake JDBC (`ANALYTICSPRD.MFG.EXENSIO_PROD_OPLOG_METADATA`), which was slow or not configured.
- **Exensio Monitoring Architecture (`ExensioLoadMonitor` + `ExensioClient`)**:
  - Exensio Monitoring uses Exensio's dedicated REST endpoint: `POST /v1/key/lot-wafer-lookup`.
  - It generates rich wafer variants (e.g. stripped prefix, 2-digit zero-padded, `lot_wafer`, `baseLot_wafer`).
  - It queries the **primary schema** (`PRODUCTION`), falling back to lot-only if wafer filter yields empty.
  - It automatically fails over to the **fallback schema** (`SANDBOX`), falling back to lot-only if wafer filter yields empty.
  - If `props.isVerifyDataLoaded()` is enabled, it verifies actual parametric test rows via the Results API (`POST /v1/result/results`).

### 2. Changes Implemented

| Component | File | Changes |
|---|---|---|
| **DTO** | [`LotVerificationResult.java`](file:///c:/Users/fg8n8x/Desktop/wip/exensioreload/backend/src/main/java/com/onsemi/cim/apps/exensio/exensioreload/dto/LotVerificationResult.java) | Added `Boolean dataVerified` field with backward-compatible 3-arg constructor. |
| **Service** | [`ExensioPreCheckService.java`](file:///c:/Users/fg8n8x/Desktop/wip/exensioreload/backend/src/main/java/com/onsemi/cim/apps/exensio/exensioreload/service/ExensioPreCheckService.java) | 1. Injected `ExensioClient` (autowired, optional).<br>2. Made `checkViaExensioLotWaferLookup` the **primary** checking path by default (matching `ExensioLoadMonitor`). Raw-SQL is only executed if `preferRawSql: true` or as a secondary fallback.<br>3. Implemented `buildExpandedWaferVariants` generating clean, zero-padded, lot-prefixed, and baseLot-prefixed wafer variants matching `ExensioClient`.<br>4. Extracted `waferKey` and `pgKey` in `parseLotWaferLookupResponse`.<br>5. Added parametric Results API check via `exensioClient.verifyDataLoaded(...)` when `isVerifyDataLoaded: true`. |
